        "root_concepts": "[braille]",
        "section": "codes",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Braille - Complete Reference",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Braille is a **6-dot tactile writing system** that encodes text and specialized notation (mathematics, music, computer data) into raised dot patterns on paper or embossed surfaces. Invented in 1824 by Louis Braille (age 15, French), it is the primary literacy system for blind and visually impaired people worldwide."
    },
    {
      "id": "02-BRAILLE.md#003",
      "path": [
        "02-BRAILLE.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:codes:02-braille, git-history:codes:02-braille]",
        "canonical_path": "codes/02-BRAILLE.md",
        "concepts": "[braille]",
        "current_path": "codes/02-BRAILLE.md",
        "id": "maxim:codes:braille",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "codes",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[braille]",
        "section": "codes",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Braille - Complete Reference",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                      BRAILLE SYSTEM MAP                          │\n│                                                                  │\n│  Grade 1 (Uncontracted)     Grade 2 (Contracted/UEB)             │\n│  ┌──────────────────┐       ┌─────────────────────┐              │\n│  │ 26 letters       │       │ Grade 1 +            │             │\n│  │ 10 digits        │  ──→  │ 189 contractions     │             │\n│  │ Punctuation      │       │ Short forms          │             │\n│  │ Basic indicators │       │ More efficient        │             │\n│  └──────────────────┘       └─────────────────────┘             │\n│                                                                  │\n│  Nemeth Code            Computer Braille (8-dot)                │\n│  ┌──────────────┐       ┌──────────────────────┐               │\n│  │ Mathematics  │       │ ASCII (256 chars)    │               │\n│  │ Science      │       │ Programming code     │               │\n│  │ Technical    │       │ Braille display out  │               │\n│  └──────────────┘       └──────────────────────┘               │\n│                                                                  │\n│  Music Braille          Braille versions exist for:             │\n│  ┌──────────────┐       Chess, Shorthand, Korean, Japanese      │\n│  │ Pitch, rhythm│       Arabic, Hebrew, Chinese, Thai...        │\n│  │ Dynamics     │       (each script has a Braille mapping)     │\n│  └──────────────┘                                               │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```"
    },
