      "text": "## The 6-Dot Cell"
    },
    {
      "id": "02-BRAILLE.md#006",
      "path": [
        "02-BRAILLE.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:codes:02-braille, git-history:codes:02-braille]",
        "canonical_path": "codes/02-BRAILLE.md",
        "concepts": "[braille]",
        "current_path": "codes/02-BRAILLE.md",
        "id": "maxim:codes:braille",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "codes",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[braille]",
        "section": "codes",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Braille - Complete Reference",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The fundamental unit of Braille is a 6-dot cell. Dots are numbered 1–6 in a fixed layout:"
    },
    {
      "id": "02-BRAILLE.md#007",
      "path": [
        "02-BRAILLE.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:codes:02-braille, git-history:codes:02-braille]",
        "canonical_path": "codes/02-BRAILLE.md",
        "concepts": "[braille]",
        "current_path": "codes/02-BRAILLE.md",
        "id": "maxim:codes:braille",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "codes",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[braille]",
        "section": "codes",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Braille - Complete Reference",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                  BRAILLE CELL LAYOUT                     │\n│                                                          │\n│    Left column    Right column                           │\n│                                                          │\n│       ● ●         Dot 1  Dot 4                           │\n│       ● ●         Dot 2  Dot 5                           │\n│       ● ●         Dot 3  Dot 6                           │\n│                                                          │\n│    Dots are named by number:                             │\n│    ·  ·  = no dots (space)                               │\n│    ●  ·  = dot 1 only → letter 'a'                       │\n│    ●  ●  = dots 1,4 → letter 'c'                         │\n│    ● ● ● = dots 1,2,3 (left column full) → 'l'           │\n│                                                          │\n│  Physical specs (BANA standard):                         │\n│  Cell width:  6.35mm    Cell height:  10.16mm            │\n│  Dot spacing: 2.34mm (center-to-center within cell)      │\n│  Inter-cell:  6.35mm (center-to-center horizontally)     │\n│  Dot height:  0.48mm above paper surface                 │\n│  Paper:       120–160 lb index stock (holds embossing)   │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "02-BRAILLE.md#008",
      "path": [
        "02-BRAILLE.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:codes:02-braille, git-history:codes:02-braille]",
        "canonical_path": "codes/02-BRAILLE.md",
        "concepts": "[braille]",
        "current_path": "codes/02-BRAILLE.md",
        "id": "maxim:codes:braille",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "codes",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[braille]",
        "section": "codes",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Braille - Complete Reference",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "With 6 binary positions, 2⁶ = **64 possible cell configurations**. Grade 1 uses 63 of them (excluding the blank). Grade 2 reuses cells with meaning determined by context and indicator cells."
    },
