        "root_concepts": "[braille]",
        "section": "codes",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Braille - Complete Reference",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Cells are described by dot numbers (e.g., \"1\" = only dot 1 raised, \"12\" = dots 1 and 2 raised):"
    },
    {
      "id": "02-BRAILLE.md#012",
      "path": [
        "02-BRAILLE.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:codes:02-braille, git-history:codes:02-braille]",
        "canonical_path": "codes/02-BRAILLE.md",
        "concepts": "[braille]",
        "current_path": "codes/02-BRAILLE.md",
        "id": "maxim:codes:braille",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "codes",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[braille]",
        "section": "codes",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Braille - Complete Reference",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│               GRADE 1 ALPHABET — DOT NUMBERS                 │\n│                                                              │\n│  a=1       b=12      c=14      d=145     e=15                │\n│  f=124     g=1245    h=125     i=24      j=245               │\n│                                                              │\n│  k=13      l=123     m=134     n=1345    o=135               │\n│  p=1234    q=12345   r=1235    s=234     t=2345              │\n│                                                              │\n│  u=136     v=1236    w=2456    x=1346    y=13456   z=1356    │\n│                                                              │\n│  PATTERN: letters a–j use only dots 1,2,4,5 (top 4 dots)     │\n│           letters k–t = corresponding a–j + dot 3            │\n│           letters u–z = corresponding k–t + dot 6            │\n│           (w is irregular: j+6 would be 2456, which IS w)    │\n│           (w was added for English; French Braille had no w) │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```"
    },
